  "notes": "More formal and institutional than {買|か}い{物|もの} (shopping). Used in economics, business, and school contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {購買力|こうばいりょく} (purchasing power)\n- {購買|こうばい}{意欲|いよく} (desire to buy)\n- {購買|こうばい}{行動|こうどう} (purchasing behavior)\n- {購買|こうばい}{部|ぶ} (purchasing department)\n\nIn schools, {購買|こうばい} (or {購買部|こうばいぶ}) often refers to the school store or co-op shop where students can buy stationery and snacks.",
